# Step one of the rock gamma calculation: what escapes the rock.
#
#   run/run_rockgamma.sh 1 40K
#
# The isotope arrives as the alias {isotope}, the way -n arrives as {nevent}, so
# one macro serves all of them and the name cannot disagree with the output file.
# Running this by hand therefore needs the alias set first:
#
#   /control/alias isotope 40K
#   /control/execute macro/rockgamma.mac
#
# U/Th/K decay inside the rock shell; every gamma that reaches the hall is written
# to an Escape tree and KILLED there. Step two then re-injects that flux on the
# hall surface, which is what a production run uses:
#
#   /gen/vertex rockgamma onvolume in Hall input data/rock_gamma.yml
#
# One isotope per run -- given as the first argument. Their activities differ and are
# measured separately, so they are weighted afterwards rather than mixed here.

# No Cherenkov or scintillation light: nothing here is an optical measurement, and
# the photons are most of the cost. Both must come before /run/initialize.
/process/optical/processActivation Cerenkov false
/process/optical/processActivation Scintillation false

/run/initialize

/run/verbose 0
/event/verbose 0
/tracking/verbose 0
/run/printProgress 1000

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What to record
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# No tracks and no steps: the Escape tree is the measurement. The Event tree still
# gets one MCPrimary per decay, which is the record of WHERE the decays were and
# what verifies the sampling -- about 47 bytes an event, so 0.5 GB at 1e7 decays.
/ROOT/savetrackopt 0
/ROOT/savestepopt 0
/ROOT/savehitphoton 0
/ROOT/savescintstep 0

# The observers. Both off unless asked for, and both change what the run does.
#
# step/rockgamma writes the Escape tree and kills each gamma as it crosses into the
# hall. An ordinary run with this on would lose the very background it is meant to
# be feeding.
/observer/step/enable rockgamma

# stack/rockgamma keeps the gammas, and the nuclei that emit them, and throws away
# every other secondary before it is tracked -- 65% of the tracks in a 40K run are
# electrons and neutrinos that only cost time. 40K: 70 s -> 5.5 s. 232Th: 177 s -> 45 s.
#
# The price, measured against the same seed: escaping gammas below 100 keV drop (40K
# loses 90% of its <50 keV, being mostly beta bremsstrahlung; 232Th loses nothing
# measurable). From 100 keV to 3 MeV every band agrees with 1 within 2 sigma in both,
# and the 1461 keV line is 1.05 +- 0.15. 100 keV cannot cross 250 mm of lead, so
# nothing this study looks at is affected. Comment it out if the soft end is the point,
# or if neutron capture gammas are -- neutrons are killed as well.
/observer/stack/enable rockgamma

/observer/list

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The source
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Rock is the shell wrapping the hall, kRockThickness deep on every face. At 1 m
# that is 10 to 20 gamma attenuation lengths, so nothing that could escape is left
# out and nothing deeper is sampled for no reason: "involume Rock" wastes nothing.
#
# 40K is a single decay with a 1.461 MeV gamma in 10.7% of them -- the clean case
# to start from.
/gen/vertex 238U involume Rock

# 238U and 232Th are CHAINS, and a chain needs thought before the number means
# anything:
#
#   - Bq/kg is normally quoted for the parent assuming secular equilibrium, i.e.
#     every daughter decaying at the parent's rate. Starting 238U and following the
#     whole chain does NOT give that in one run, because the daughters carry their
#     real half-lives -- 226Ra alone is 1600 years.
#   - The usual way is to run the chain in segments and add them with equal
#     activity, restricting each with
#       /process/had/rdm/nucleusLimits <aMin> <aMax> <zMin> <zMax>
#     Most of the gamma yield is in the lower part of each chain: 214Pb and 214Bi
#     for 238U, 212Pb, 212Bi and 208Tl for 232Th.
#
#   run/run_rockgamma.sh 1 238U
#   run/run_rockgamma.sh 1 232Th



/run/beamOn {nevent}
